# What must never be uploaded to a build.
#
# The CLI does not apply .gitignore the way the git integration does, so
# `vercel --prod` was packing data/, which holds a 188 MB corpus of the client's
# own mail (data/corpus/sweep-threads.jsonl). It failed with "File size limit
# exceeded (100 MB)" — which is the good outcome; the bad one is the version of
# that file small enough to succeed, quietly shipping client correspondence into a
# deployment that does not need it. Nothing here is read at runtime: the engine
# reads its data from Neon and OnSinch.
data/
.tmp-data/
n8n/backups/
sim/
test/
scripts/
docs/
fleet/
*.log
